# logging

trueos_cabi_log(level,target_ptr,target_len,message_ptr,message_len) sends one already formatted UTF-8 record to the host log router, separate from attached-terminal bytes. No format string or Rust fmt::Arguments crosses this ABI. Level constants are listed below. Target must be nonempty and at most 256 bytes; message limit is 65536 bytes. Hull transport can truncate long messages to its payload capacity on a UTF-8 boundary. Return0 indicates accepted normal submission; negative indicates error, not necessarily delivery to every configured sink.

LOG_FLAG_QUERY_ENABLED ORed into the level queries filtering with an empty message:1 enabled,0 disabled,negative unsupported/error. LOG_LEVEL_ONCE carries no stable guest callsite identity.

trueos_cabi_write uses stream1 stdout and2 stderr, accepting already prepared bytes. Use terminal.prm for screen drawing. A small local Odin formatting module is needed for dynamic numbers, floats, padding or interpolation; logging does not provide that formatting.



